WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:04.253
Sam Naidoo: Morning, everyone.

2
00:00:04.253 --> 00:00:05.983
Sam Naidoo: Thanks for making the time.

3
00:00:05.983 --> 00:00:09.891
Sam Naidoo: Before we start, I'd like to confirm what we agreed by email.

4
00:00:09.891 --> 00:00:17.194
Sam Naidoo: I'm using the meeting's transcript to write up the requirements, and the AI that helps me runs on my own computer.

5
00:00:17.194 --> 00:00:19.500
Sam Naidoo: Is that still fine with both of you?

6
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.400
Thandi Mokoena: Yes, that's fine with me.

7
00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:24.600
Pieter van Wyk: Ja, fine.

8
00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:27.530
Sam Naidoo: Thank you.

9
00:00:27.530 --> 00:00:33.740
Sam Naidoo: So the goal today is to understand how dispatch works now and what the app has to do.

10
00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:37.100
Sam Naidoo: Thandi, do you want to start with the problem?

11
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:38.414
Thandi Mokoena: Sure.

12
00:00:38.414 --> 00:00:46.849
Thandi Mokoena: We run forty trucks between Gauteng and the Western Cape, out of two depots, Midrand and Bloemfontein.

13
00:00:46.849 --> 00:00:49.248
Thandi Mokoena: Dispatch happens on WhatsApp.

14
00:00:49.248 --> 00:01:00.330
Thandi Mokoena: The controller posts the collections in a group, the drivers reply, and then somebody types it all into a shared spreadsheet at night.

15
00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:04.300
Thandi Mokoena: We miss collections because messages get buried.

16
00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:08.000
Sam Naidoo: How many collections is that on a normal day?

17
00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:11.857
Thandi Mokoena: About a hundred and twenty a day.

18
00:01:11.857 --> 00:01:15.400
Thandi Mokoena: In November and December it roughly doubles.

19
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:20.600
Pieter van Wyk: On the bad days in December we've had two hundred and sixty.

20
00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.200
Sam Naidoo: And what does a missed collection cost you?

21
00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:33.252
Thandi Mokoena: A re-delivery is about eighteen hundred rand, and we lose the client's trust, which is worse.

22
00:01:33.252 --> 00:01:37.600
Thandi Mokoena: Last December we lost one retail account over it.

23
00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:42.673
Sam Naidoo: So the app has to make sure every collection is assigned and confirmed.

24
00:01:42.673 --> 00:01:45.200
Sam Naidoo: What does a driver need to do on the road?

25
00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:53.985
Pieter van Wyk: Accept the job, mark it collected, take a photo of the waybill, and get a signature.

26
00:01:53.985 --> 00:02:02.446
Pieter van Wyk: But you must understand, between Colesberg and Beaufort West there's no signal for hours.

27
00:02:02.446 --> 00:02:09.100
Pieter van Wyk: It has to work offline and send everything when they're back in range.

28
00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.128
Sam Naidoo: That's an important constraint.

29
00:02:12.128 --> 00:02:14.600
Sam Naidoo: Do the drivers all have smartphones?

30
00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:18.229
Pieter van Wyk: Most have Android phones, their own.

31
00:02:18.229 --> 00:02:21.846
Pieter van Wyk: I think they all do, but I'd have to check.

32
00:02:21.846 --> 00:02:25.800
Pieter van Wyk: A few of the older guys still use basic phones.

33
00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:30.400
Thandi Mokoena: We'd rather not buy phones for everyone if we can avoid it.

34
00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:31.856
Sam Naidoo: Understood.

35
00:02:31.856 --> 00:02:35.200
Sam Naidoo: Which systems would this have to work with?

36
00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:41.597
Thandi Mokoena: Our trucks have a tracking system from a vendor, so we can see where they are.

37
00:02:41.597 --> 00:02:43.535
Thandi Mokoena: And invoicing runs on Sage.

38
00:02:43.535 --> 00:02:51.500
Thandi Mokoena: It would be nice if the app could pull positions from the tracking system, but it's not essential at the start.

39
00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:55.000
Sam Naidoo: Who decides on the budget for this?

40
00:02:55.800 --> 00:03:01.864
Thandi Mokoena: Our MD signs off anything above two hundred thousand rand.

41
00:03:01.864 --> 00:03:07.300
Thandi Mokoena: I'd want to show her a figure by the end of January.

42
00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:11.735
Lerato Dlamini: Sorry I'm late, I was stuck in another call.

43
00:03:11.735 --> 00:03:15.600
Lerato Dlamini: I look after their network and the depot computers.

44
00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:17.065
Sam Naidoo: Welcome, Lerato.

45
00:03:17.065 --> 00:03:19.174
Sam Naidoo: We were just talking about offline use.

46
00:03:19.174 --> 00:03:21.500
Sam Naidoo: How reliable is the internet at the depots?

47
00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:23.681
Lerato Dlamini: Midrand is fine.

48
00:03:23.681 --> 00:03:31.534
Lerato Dlamini: Bloemfontein goes down during load-shedding because the router isn't on the backup battery.

49
00:03:31.534 --> 00:03:34.900
Lerato Dlamini: That should be fixed, but it isn't yet.

50
00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:39.200
Pieter van Wyk: And when it's down, the controller can't see anything.

51
00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:44.817
Sam Naidoo: Then the controller's screen needs to cope with the depot being offline too.

52
00:03:44.817 --> 00:03:45.768
Sam Naidoo: One more thing.

53
00:03:45.768 --> 00:03:48.557
Sam Naidoo: Drivers' locations are personal information.

54
00:03:48.557 --> 00:03:51.600
Sam Naidoo: Have you checked how you're allowed to use them?

55
00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:53.265
Thandi Mokoena: Not yet.

56
00:03:53.265 --> 00:03:59.100
Thandi Mokoena: HR would have to look at that with the drivers' union.

57
00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.040
Sam Naidoo: I'll note it as an open question.

58
00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:06.800
Sam Naidoo: Last thing: is there anything you'd want later, but not in the first version?

59
00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:12.662
Thandi Mokoena: Eventually our clients should get a tracking link, like a courier.

60
00:04:12.662 --> 00:04:13.600
Thandi Mokoena: But not now.

61
00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:16.481
Pieter van Wyk: And Afrikaans in the app.

62
00:04:16.481 --> 00:04:19.400
Pieter van Wyk: Half my drivers would prefer it.

63
00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:20.316
Sam Naidoo: Good.

64
00:04:20.316 --> 00:04:26.753
Sam Naidoo: My suggestion is to start with a pilot at the Bloemfontein depot, since it has the hardest conditions.

65
00:04:26.753 --> 00:04:27.700
Sam Naidoo: Does that work?

66
00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:31.500
Thandi Mokoena: Yes, let's do Bloemfontein first.

67
00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:32.630
Sam Naidoo: Great.

68
00:04:32.630 --> 00:04:36.302
Sam Naidoo: I'll send a summary this afternoon.

69
00:04:36.302 --> 00:04:38.400
Sam Naidoo: Thank you, everyone.
